# JVM options for Open Liberty — Próximo Pitido server
#
# --enable-native-access: granted to ALL-UNNAMED because Liberty's OSGi classloader
# loads application JARs onto the classpath at runtime.
# Even though codecs/input and codecs/sip carry module-info.java (compile-time named
# modules), the JVM sees them as part of the unnamed module under Liberty's OSGi bundle
# classloading — named module identifiers are not visible at runtime in this deployment
# model.
# Using ALL-UNNAMED is therefore the correct value; module-info.java still enforces
# encapsulation and dependency declarations at compile time.
--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED

# Suppress unknown-flag warnings when running on HotSpot so that OpenJ9-specific
# tuning flags below are silently ignored instead of aborting startup.
-XX:+IgnoreUnrecognizedVMOptions

# OpenJ9 container tuning — silently ignored on HotSpot.
# ClassRelationshipVerifier: lazy class verification reduces startup time.
# Xtune:virtualize: optimise for a virtualised or container host.
-XX:+ClassRelationshipVerifier
-Xtune:virtualize

# Heap bounds — gencon (the OpenJ9 default) with explicit min/max.
# -Xms: minimum heap kept at all times; prevents over-shrinkage between calls.
# -Xmx: maximum heap; sized for Liberty (~60 MB) plus 4 concurrent calls
#        (~20 MB each for audio buffers, codec state, and RTP queues) plus margin.
# -Xmn: nursery fixed at 32 MB; keeps scavenge pauses short and predictable
#        without requiring GC policy tuning flags.
-Xms96m
-Xmx256m
-Xmn32m
